IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sazwt-law`
IMPORT `sazwt-seat`

-- Cases for the seat layer (sazwt-seat.l4): a soldier serving within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence, not posted to an annex establishment,
-- not in a § 30c(4) activity, below pay grade B 6. Expected values are written from SAZV §§ 5, 6 and 12 as deposited, in both versions, not from this encoding's output.
-- Each "if void" question takes, last, whether an exception to the citation requirement applies: FALSE gives the earlier wording, TRUE the 2025 wording.

§ `Case A: a full-time soldier whose unit needs a Sunday`

-- As printed, service reasons allow any departure from Monday to Friday; on the earlier wording, only as far as Saturday.
#ASSERT `over which days may my weekly working time be distributed as printed` 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST `any days of the week`
#ASSERT `over which days may my weekly working time be distributed if the 2025 amendment is void` 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Monday to Saturday`
#ASSERT `over which days may my weekly working time be distributed if the 2025 amendment is void` 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `any days of the week`
-- Without service reasons, Monday to Friday either way.
#ASSERT `over which days may my weekly working time be distributed if the 2025 amendment is void` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Monday to Friday`

§ `Case B: a part-time soldier, working time reduced by half, who applies for an individual distribution`

-- As printed, it may be approved unless service reasons stand against it; the earlier wording has no such sentence and does not reach this soldier at all.
#ASSERT `may an individual distribution be approved on my application as printed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `may an individual distribution be approved on my application as printed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `may an individual distribution be approved on my application if the 2025 amendment is void` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `may an individual distribution be approved on my application if the 2025 amendment is void` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `over which days may my weekly working time be distributed if the 2025 amendment is void` 50 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `over which days may my weekly working time be distributed as printed` 50 FALSE EQUALS JUST `Monday to Friday`

§ `Case C: fifteen hours on a permanent operational task`

-- Service reasons require it; the continuity of the service need not be ensured; nothing out of the ordinary has happened.
-- As printed, none of nos. 1 to 3 covers it, so the 13 hours hold. On the earlier wording, Dauereinsatzaufgaben is named and service reasons suffice:
-- if the 2025 recast is void, the soldier may be kept longer.
#ASSERT NOT (`is my daily working time today allowed as printed` 15 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `is my daily working time today allowed if the 2025 amendment is void` 15 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`is my daily working time today allowed if the 2025 amendment is void` 15 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `on which ground may my daily working time today exceed 13 hours as printed` TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
#ASSERT `on which ground may my daily working time today exceed 13 hours if the 2025 amendment is void` TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list names`

§ `Case D: fourteen hours of close protection duty`

-- As printed, no. 1 names it; on the earlier wording it is not named, but service reasons suffice.
#ASSERT `is my daily working time today allowed as printed` 14 TRUE `military police duty (Feldjägerdienst) or close protection (Personenschutzdienst)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `is my daily working time today allowed if the 2025 amendment is void` 14 TRUE `military police duty (Feldjägerdienst) or close protection (Personenschutzdienst)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `on which ground may my daily working time today exceed 13 hours as printed` TRUE `military police duty (Feldjägerdienst) or close protection (Personenschutzdienst)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 1 as printed: guard, special, orderly or military police duty`
-- Without service reasons, neither wording lets the day exceed 13 hours.
#ASSERT NOT (`is my daily working time today allowed if the 2025 amendment is void` 14 FALSE `military police duty (Feldjägerdienst) or close protection (Personenschutzdienst)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Case E: 34 hours on call in a month, compelling service reasons blocking three hours of compensation`

-- One eighth of the 24 hours above 10 is 3 hours. As printed, the three blocked hours take it to 0; on the earlier wording service reasons do not reduce it.
#ASSERT `how many hours of compensation am I owed for on-call duty as printed` 34 0 3 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `how many hours of compensation am I owed for on-call duty if the 2025 amendment is void` 34 0 3 FALSE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `how many hours of compensation am I owed for on-call duty if the 2025 amendment is void` 34 0 3 TRUE EQUALS 0
-- With nothing blocked, 3 hours either way; with 10 of the 34 hours actually called on, 24 count and the answer is 1.75.
#ASSERT `how many hours of compensation am I owed for on-call duty as printed` 34 0 0 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `how many hours of compensation am I owed for on-call duty as printed` 34 10 0 EQUALS 1.75

§ `Case F: the form of the compensation`

#ASSERT `in what form is the compensation for on-call duty given` `fixed working time` EQUALS `time off (Dienstbefreiung)`
#ASSERT `in what form is the compensation for on-call duty given` `flexitime (Gleitzeit)` EQUALS `a credit to the flexitime account`

§ `Case G: the preamble`

-- The fact the voidness argument turns on, and the fact that makes it contestable.
#ASSERT NOT (`does the 2025 preamble cite the power over regular working time`)
#ASSERT `does the 2025 preamble name section 93(2) no. 6`
